WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.871
Context selection is the act of choosing what the model actually needs for the task.

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:08.180
More information is not always better.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.028
Start by identifying the decision, question, or artifact you want.

00:00:12.028 --> 00:00:15.490
Then include the source material that directly supports it.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:20.108
Remove duplicates, stale drafts, irrelevant examples, and material that only adds noise.

00:00:20.108 --> 00:00:23.955
Selection is often more valuable than simply expanding the prompt.

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:27.033
Compression means reducing material while preserving what matters.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:31.266
A useful summary can keep key facts, decisions, assumptions, constraints, evidence,

00:00:31.266 --> 00:00:33.959
and open questions while leaving out repetition.

00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:36.652
Conversation history often benefits from periodic summarization.

00:00:36.652 --> 00:00:39.730
Long documents may benefit from outlines, section summaries,

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:43.193
or extracted requirements before the full text is included.

00:00:43.193 --> 00:00:45.117
Over-compression is a real risk.

00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:49.350
If a summary removes uncertainty, exceptions, minority opinions, or evidence trails,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.351
the model may produce an answer that sounds confident but misses important nuance.

00:00:54.351 --> 00:00:57.814
Compression should preserve the information needed for the task,

00:00:57.814 --> 00:01:00.123
not merely make the text shorter.

00:01:00.123 --> 00:01:01.277
For high-stakes work,

00:01:01.277 --> 00:01:07.049
keep links or citations back to the original material so reviewers can verify the summary.

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:08.588
Staged prompting can help.

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:11.666
First ask for an outline, inventory, or summary.

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:15.513
Then ask for a focused analysis using that prepared context.

00:01:15.513 --> 00:01:19.746
For complex workflows, maintain a versioned project summary that includes decisions,

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.439
open questions, current assumptions, and excluded material.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.056
This gives the model a compact but useful working memory without forcing

00:01:27.056 --> 00:01:28.980
every request to include everything.
